{title: Rock of Ages}
{title_ko: 만세 반석 열리니}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 494장}
{artist: Augustus Toplady / Thomas Hastings}
{genre: Hymn}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: D}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 3/4}
{score: rock-of-ages.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Rock of Ages, [G]cleft for [D]me
Let me [A]hide myself in [D]Thee
Let the [D]water and the [G]blood
From Thy [D]wounded side which [A]flowed
Be of [D]sin the double [Bm]cure
Save from [G]wrath and make me [A]pure [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Not the labors [G]of my [D]hands
Can ful[A]fill Thy law's de[D]mands
Could my [D]zeal no respite [G]know
Could my [D]tears forever [A]flow
All for [D]sin could not a[Bm]tone
Thou must [G]save, and Thou a[A]lone [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Nothing in my [G]hand I [D]bring
Simply [A]to Thy cross I [D]cling
Naked, [D]come to Thee for [G]dress
Helpless, [D]look to Thee for [A]grace
Foul, I [D]to the fountain [Bm]fly
Wash me, [G]Savior, or I [A]die [D]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]While I draw this [G]fleeting [D]breath
When mine [A]eyes shall close in [D]death
When I [D]rise to worlds un[G]known
And be[D]hold Thee on Thy [A]throne
Rock of [D]Ages, cleft for [Bm]me
Let me [G]hide myself in [A]Thee [D]
{end_of_verse}
